|> game and by trial and error try to get the good gifts of the throne. If you get
|> one (for example: an ability or a wish) and the throne does not vanish, refresh
|> your save file. Do not waste wishes for getting abilities. You can get nearly
|> everything you want. The only disadvantage is : it takes so much time.
|> But it makes the game so much easier.
|> 
|> If you save your game in the same manner as above, you can test by trial and
|> error, if the next level is the one you want to play. If not, try another.
|> The only fixed level in every special game is the castle.

Doesn't sound like a spoiler, sounds like save restore abuse.

If you do that much saving and restoring, there's no way you'll ever
lose.  You could do the same before drinking a glowing potion.  When
you get a wish, you could do the same until you really get a +3 Stormy,
or whatever.  In fact, you could save on level 1 just before you go
down the stairs, and then keep saving and restoring until eventually
a wand of wishing appears in the first room of level 2.  It'll only take
a million or so save / restores :)

Seriously, if you're that desperate to win, why not just play in discover
mode?

